The patch misses the case where vector kinds persist across sessions: writes made without an embedder after a prior live vector declaration can be terminally failed instead of deferred/grafted. This violates the new graceful-absent contract and can leave rows permanently without vectors.

Review comment:

- [P1] Do not enqueue vector work in no-embedder sessions — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s20c/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17264-17270
  When a database already has a persisted vector-kind row from an earlier live-embedder session, opening it with `EmbedderChoice::None` and writing that kind still reaches this `kind_is_vector_indexed` check and enqueues projection work. The no-embedder worker records an `EmbedderNotConfiguredError`/`failed` terminal, and the later graft path only reopens `up_to_date` stranded rows, so reopening with an embedder leaves that write permanently unembedded while readiness can return ready. The live-embedder gate needs to apply to enqueueing as well as late enrolment/backfill.
The patch misses the case where vector kinds persist across sessions: writes made without an embedder after a prior live vector declaration can be terminally failed instead of deferred/grafted. This violates the new graceful-absent contract and can leave rows permanently without vectors.

